MINION 3
#FAIL
#TEST SOLCOUNT 0
# Regression: gccweak shares gcc's matching structures and the same aliasing
# limitation, so it likewise refuses a counted/cardinality aliased variable.
**VARIABLES**
DISCRETE x {-10..9}
BOOL b
DISCRETE c {-7..2}
**SEARCH**
PRINT[[x],[b],[c]]
**CONSTRAINTS**
gccweak([x, x], [4, -9], [b, c])
**EOF**
